          <article style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#ddd;">
            <div class="lead" style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.6;margin-bottom:32px;color:#bbb;">
              Launching a new website is exciting; what comes after is what determines whether it generates revenue. This is the 90-day digital marketing checklist we walk every new client through — the foundations that, if skipped, cost you 3-6 months of compounded growth.
            </div>
            <style>article a {color:rgb(20,120,190);text-decoration:underline;} article h2 {margin-top:48px;} article h3 {margin-top:32px;}</style>
            <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Days 1-7 — Technical foundations (one-time)</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Install Google Analytics 4</strong> — measure baseline traffic before any campaigns</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Install Meta Pixel</strong> + Google Tag Manager — enables future paid retargeting</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Set up Google Search Console</strong> — verify site, submit XML sitemap</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Set up Bing Webmaster Tools</strong> — small traffic share but free signal</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Install Microsoft Clarity</strong> — heatmaps + session replays (free)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Test Core Web Vitals</strong> — Lighthouse mobile score 90+</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Set up 301 redirects</strong> if migrating from an old site (preserves SEO equity)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Configure SSL + force HTTPS</strong> — non-negotiable in 2026</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Test mobile experience</strong> on 3 real devices (iPhone, Android, tablet)</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Days 8-14 — SEO foundations</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Keyword research:</strong> 30-50 primary + secondary keywords mapped to specific pages</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>On-page optimization:</strong> unique title tag + meta description per page</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Schema markup:</strong> Organization, LocalBusiness (if local), Service, BreadcrumbList, FAQPage where relevant</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Image alt text:</strong> descriptive, keyword-aware for every image</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Internal linking:</strong> at least 3-5 contextual internal links per page</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>XML sitemap:</strong> auto-generated, submitted to Search Console</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Robots.txt:</strong> clean, with sitemap reference</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Days 15-30 — Local SEO (if applicable)</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Google Business Profile:</strong> claim, verify, fully populate (see our <a href="../local-seo-pakistani-businesses/">local SEO blog</a>)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Bing Places:</strong> claim + verify</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Apple Maps Connect:</strong> claim listing</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Top 10 citations:</strong> NAP-consistent across the major directories</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>First 5-10 Google reviews:</strong> reach out to past customers</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Days 30-45 — Content engine kickoff</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Launch a blog</strong> with 3-5 cornerstone articles (1,500-2,500 words each)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Service-page content review:</strong> each service has 600+ words with FAQ section</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Add real testimonials</strong> with photos + full names + companies</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Case study creation:</strong> 1-2 detailed case studies</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>About page:</strong> team photos + bios with Person schema</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Days 30-60 — Paid ads launch</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Define one clear conversion goal</strong> (form fill, purchase, demo booked)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Build 2-3 dedicated landing pages</strong> for ad campaigns</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Launch Google Search Ads</strong> on 5-10 high-intent keywords (start small)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Launch Meta Ads</strong> (if relevant to your business)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Set up conversion tracking</strong> in both platforms with Conversions API for Meta</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Monitor weekly</strong> — kill underperformers fast</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Days 45-75 — Email + retention loops</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Set up email service:</strong> Mailchimp, Brevo, Klaviyo (for e-commerce)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Welcome series:</strong> 4-7 emails over 14 days for new subscribers</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Newsletter cadence:</strong> weekly or bi-weekly content schedule</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Abandoned cart flow</strong> (for e-commerce)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Post-purchase follow-up</strong> (review request, cross-sell)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Lead magnet creation:</strong> ebook, checklist, or template to grow email list</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Days 60-90 — Measurement + iteration</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>First monthly performance review:</strong> what's working, what to kill, what to scale</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Identify top 3 traffic sources</strong> and double down</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Identify top 3 conversion paths</strong> and optimize</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Run first A/B test</strong> on highest-traffic landing page</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Refresh content</strong> based on what's ranking and what's converting</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Plan Q2 (next 90 days)</strong> based on real data, not assumptions</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">What most new websites skip (and pay for later)</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Skipping Search Console setup</strong> — you find out about issues 6 months later</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Skipping schema markup</strong> — leaves rich-result CTR on the table</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Skipping email capture from day 1</strong> — losing potential audience daily</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Skipping speed optimization</strong> — every 100ms costs ~1% of conversion</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Skipping mobile testing</strong> — 70%+ of your traffic is mobile</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Skipping case studies</strong> — buyers need proof before they buy</li></ul>
            <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4 mt-5">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">How much does this 90-day setup cost?</h3><p>DIY: USD 500-1,500 in tool costs. Agency-run (full execution): USD 3,000-15,000 depending on scope. Apex Marketings typically runs new-site clients through this for USD 4,000-8,000 over 90 days, then transitions to a monthly retainer.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">Can I skip paid ads in the first 90 days?</h3><p>Yes if you have 6+ months of runway and trust <a href="/services/seo-services/" style="text-decoration:underline;">SEO</a> to compound. Most growing businesses need paid ads for cash flow during the SEO ramp-up period.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">What if my website is brand new with zero traffic?</h3><p>Expect 4-6 months before <a href="/services/seo-services/" style="text-decoration:underline;">SEO</a> produces meaningful organic traffic. Paid ads can produce traffic immediately. Plan budgets accordingly.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">What's the single most important item on this list?</h3><p>Setting up GA4 + Search Console + Meta Pixel from day one. If you don't have measurement infrastructure, you can't optimize what you can't measure.</p>
